    <div style="flex: 1;">
      <div class="section-title">CSUN SUSTAINABILITY CENTER</div>
      <p>The Associated Students (AS) at California State University, Northridge (CSUN) has de-signed and constructed a new {{ center_name }} Sustainability Center. The new AS Sus-tainability Center is a multi-functional space, serving primarily as an expanded central col-lection space for campus recyclables. It also serves as the public face and administrative hub of the Center for its programs and services. In addition, it is home to the administration of the {{ center_department }} and the {{ center_office }} office. The Center is a beacon of sustainability for the university community, providing a dedicated space for environmental programs, services and issues related to the environment and sustainability. The Center will also serve as a meeting space for student organizations, faculty, and staff. The Center is designed to be a zero-net-energy building, meaning that solar panels will be the main source of electricity. The Sustainability Cen-ter will also feature a large collection of recycled materials, providing a visible reminder of the importance of sustainability. The building also includes administrative offices, shower rooms and a com-posting toilet.</p>
      <img src="placeholder_sustainability_center.jpg" alt="Sustainability Center" style="width: 100%; margin-top: 15px;">
      <p style="font-size: 9pt; text-align: center; margin-top: 5px;">Gensler | California State University, Northridge | Associated Students Sustainability Center</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 40px;">
      <div style="flex: 1;">
        <div class="section-title">FACULTY PUBLICATIONS</div>
        <div class="list-item">
