        </div>
        <div class="list-item">
          <span data-field="publication.title_3">{{ publication.title_3 }}</span>, <span data-field="publication.authors_3">{{ publication.authors_3 }}</span>, <span data-field="publication.journal_3">{{ publication.journal_3 }}</span>, {{ publication.year_3 }}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="flex: 1;">
        <div class="section-title">COMMUNITY PARTNERS: THE CITY OF LOS ANGELES</div>
        <p>The City of Los Angeles has long been an important community partner for the Department of Urban Studies and Planning. This has been especially true with respect to the Planning Department as well as the planning staff employed independently by the city councilmembers in the City of Los Angeles. The department has worked closely with the City of Los Angeles on various projects, including the {{ project_name_1 }} (in Spring {{ year_1 }}) and {{ project_name_2 }} (in Fall {{ year_2 }}). Christina Nguyen ({{ cg_id }}) in Spring {{ year_1 }} and Alvaro Barbagan in Fall {{ year_2 }}. City planners, Elena Nuno-Odommel and Adam Vallan, have done a superb job supporting and mentoring these interns. The city also provided many other internship opportunities. Many students have also found rewarding planning internships working in the district offices of Los Angeles City Councilmembers. Alumni Patricia Steyer ({{ ps_id }}), Claudia Rodriguez ({{ cr_id }}), Andy Rodriguez ({{ ar_id }}), Dana Yedoyan ({{ dy_id }}), Sergio Carvalho ({{ sc_id }}), and others have worked with the City of Los Angeles. The department of Transportation and Humberto Quintana ({{ hq_id }}) in the Mayor's office. Many CSUN graduates also pursued their careers with the City of Los Angeles in planning and related fields. These include Alena James ({{ aj_id }}), John Strickland ({{ js_id }}), Anna Vidal ({{ av_id }}), Claudia Rodriguez ({{ cr_id }}), Andy Rodriguez ({{ ar_id }}), Alisha Marshall ({{ am_id }}), and Karapatian ({{ k_id }}), Hatim Fateh ({{ hf_id }}), Ruben Rubi ({{ rr_id }}) and Olga Ayala ({{ oa_id }}).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
